BM-STF release — third-party notices and provenance

This repository carries no third-party code. It depends on, and where noted
cites, the following externally maintained material. Versions below are the
ones reported by the manuscript's executed in-silico study or the ones this release
is tested against.

Runtime dependencies
--------------------
NumPy                 BSD-3-Clause    https://numpy.org/            >=2.0,<3
SciPy                 BSD-3-Clause    https://scipy.org/            >=1.14,<2
scikit-learn          BSD-3-Clause    https://scikit-learn.org/     >=1.5,<2
PyYAML                MIT             https://pyyaml.org/           >=6.0,<7

The manuscript reports the analysis environment as Python 3.9.6 with
NumPy 2.0.2 (Code availability). This release targets Python >= 3.10 with the
dependency ranges above; see claim_to_code.json for the recorded deviation.

Cited imaging and hemodynamic resources
--------------------------------------
AAA-100 and AAA-L regenerated CFD sets, Rygiel et al.,
  "Wall Shear Stress Estimation in Abdominal Aortic Aneurysms: Towards
  Generalisable Neural Surrogate Models", arXiv:2507.22817.
  Used as the surrogate-substrate parity comparators of Table 5 panel B. The
  release does not redistribute the meshes or solver fields.

Merlin CT vision-language foundation model, Blankemeier et al., Nature.
  Cited as the frozen abdominal-CT embedding used as image context by the
  hazard head. Weights are not redistributed here.

Intracranial geometry stress-test set, Lannelongue et al.,
  npj Digital Medicine 9, 212 (2026).
  Used by the manuscript as a cross-anatomy stress test only.

Clinical cohorts (not redistributed)
-----------------------------------
The retrospective supporting cohort and the silent-mode arm described in
